{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% import "macros.html.j2" as m %}
{% block content %}
{% set latest = years[-1] %}
{% set p = pooled or latest %}
{% set h = highlights %}
{% macro pct(v, d=1) %}{{ ("%." ~ d ~ "f")|format(100 * v) }}%{% endmacro %}
{% macro x(v) %}{{ "%.1f"|format(v) }}×{% endmacro %}
{% macro rate_table(t, head, sub=None) %}
<div class="scroll"><table class="hl-table rates">
<thead><tr><th class="text">{{ head }}</th><th>Talks / abstracts</th><th class="text">Talk rate · 95% CI</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for r in t.rows %}<tr><td class="text">{{ r.label }}{% if sub %}<span class="related">{{ r[sub] }}</span>{% endif %}</td>
<td>{{ r.talks }} / {{ r.abstracts }}</td>
<td class="text"><span class="rate"><span class="track">
<span class="ci" style="left:{{ '%.1f'|format(r.ci_left) }}%;width:{{ '%.1f'|format(r.ci_width) }}%"></span>
<span class="pt" style="left:{{ '%.1f'|format(r.bar) }}%"></span>
<span class="base" style="left:{{ '%.1f'|format(t.base) }}%"></span></span>
<span class="val">{{ pct(r.talk_rate) }}</span></span></td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody></table></div>
{% endmacro %}
<h1>{{ page.title }}</h1>
<p class="lede">Every year the American Society of Human Genetics picks a few hundred of its several thousand accepted
abstracts for a talk; the rest become posters. This site parses the published abstracts
({{ years[0].year }}–{{ latest.year }}{% if pooled %}: {{ "{:,}".format(p.summary.abstracts) }} abstracts,
{{ "{:,}".format(p.summary.talks) }} talks{% endif %}) and asks which phrases, institutions and places show up more
often among talks.</p>
<p class="caveat"><strong>Read this first.</strong> The abstracts list only <em>accepted</em> work, and authors
can ask for a poster. “Talk rate” is the fraction of accepted abstracts presented as a talk, not an acceptance
rate or a quality score. Every number here is an association. Not every affiliation could be matched to an
institution or place: see the <a href="methods.html#match-rates">match rates</a>.</p>

{% if h %}
<section class="vignette" id="hot">
<h2><span class="num">1</span>What's hot at ASHG {{ h.latest }}</h2>
{% set r0 = h.rising[0] %}
<p class="lead">Topics that keep growing: “{{ r0.phrase }}” is in {{ pct(r0.last) }} of {{ h.latest }} abstracts, up
from {{ pct(r0.first) }} in {{ years[0].year }}.</p>
<div class="scroll"><table class="hl-table">
<thead><tr><th class="text">Topic</th><th>{{ years[0].year }}</th><th class="text spark-col">{{ years[0].year }}–{{ h.latest }}</th>
<th>{{ h.latest }}</th><th>Talks in {{ h.latest }}</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for r in h.rising %}<tr><td class="text">{{ r.phrase }}</td><td>{{ pct(r.first) }}</td><td class="text spark-col">{{ r.spark }}</td>
<td><strong>{{ pct(r.last) }}</strong></td><td>{{ r.talks_last }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody></table></div>
<p class="table-note">Share of each year's accepted abstracts mentioning the topic (title or text; spelling variants count).</p>
<p><strong>Most talk-leaning in {{ h.latest }}</strong> (phrases in at least 10 talks):
{% for r in h.hot %}“{{ r.ngram }}” {{ x(r["or"]) }}{{ ", " if not loop.last else "." }}{% endfor %} (Odds of a talk with versus without
the phrase.)</p>
{% if h.shift %}
<p><strong>Clinical work stopped leaning toward posters.</strong> Through {{ years[-2].year }},
{% for r in h.shift %}“{{ r.phrase }}”{{ " and " if not loop.last else "" }}{% endfor %} came up more often in posters
than in talks; in {{ h.latest }} they leaned toward talks:
{% for r in h.shift %}“{{ r.phrase }}” {{ "%.2f"|format(r.or_before) }}× → {{ "%.2f"|format(r.or_last) }}× (p = {{ "%.3f"|format(r.p) }}){{ ", " if not loop.last else "." }}{% endfor %}</p>
{% endif %}
<p class="more-link"><a href="phrases.html">Phrase trends, each year's top phrases and a lookup for any phrase →</a></p>
</section>

<section class="vignette" id="institutions">
<h2><span class="num">2</span>Institutions with the highest talk rate</h2>
{% set i3 = h.inst.rows[:3] %}
<p class="lead">Among the {{ h.inst_pool }} institutions with the most first-author abstracts ({{ p.label }}),
{{ i3[0].label }}, {{ i3[1].label }} and {{ i3[2].label }} lead, at {{ pct(i3[2].talk_rate, 0) }}–{{ pct(i3[0].talk_rate, 0) }}
of abstracts given a talk, against {{ pct(h.baseline) }} overall.</p>
{{ rate_table(h.inst, "Institution") }}
<p class="table-note">First author's institutions; dashed line = all abstracts ({{ pct(h.baseline) }}). Smaller
institutions have wide intervals. In {{ h.latest }} alone, {{ h.latest_top | join(", ") }} had the highest rates.</p>
<p class="more-link"><a href="institutions.html">All 50 largest institutions, year by year →</a></p>
</section>

<section class="vignette" id="authors">
<h2><span class="num">3</span>Senior authors with the best record</h2>
{% set most = h.author_most %}
<p class="lead">Ranked by the lower end of a 95% interval, so a long record beats a short lucky one (at least
{{ h.author_min }} abstracts as senior author, {{ p.label }}). {{ most.name }} ({{ most.institute }}) has the most talks:
{{ most.talks }} of {{ most.abstracts }}.</p>
{{ rate_table(h.authors, "Senior author", "institute") }}
<p class="table-note">Last listed author; dashed line = all abstracts. The {{ years[0].year }}–2024 abstracts give only
initials, so across years one person is first initial + last name (common surnames also need a shared institution).</p>
<p class="more-link"><a href="authors.html">The full ranking, year by year →</a></p>
</section>

{% if h.center %}
<section class="vignette" id="center">
<h2><span class="num">4</span>The center of mass follows the host city</h2>
{% set pulls = h.center | sort(attribute="km", reverse=True) %}
<p class="lead">Local groups bring extra abstracts to a home meeting. Leave out first authors from the host city and the
center of mass of North American abstracts moves {{ "{:,}".format(pulls[0].km) }} km for {{ pulls[0].host }}
{{ pulls[0].year }}, and {{ pulls[-1].km }} km for {{ pulls[-1].host }} {{ pulls[-1].year }}.</p>
{% if "trends_center_na" in trends %}
{{ m.figure("img/trends_center_na.png", "Map of North America and a zoom on Illinois and Indiana, with the yearly center of US and Canadian first authors' metro areas moving toward each year's host city.") }}
{% endif %}
<p class="table-note">Host-city pull by year:
{% for r in h.center %}{{ r.host }} {{ r.year }} {{ "{:,}".format(r.km) }} km{{ " · " if not loop.last else "." }}{% endfor %}</p>
<p class="more-link"><a href="geography.html#center">Interactive map: talks, worldwide, without North America →</a></p>
</section>
{% endif %}
{% endif %}

<h2 id="explore">Explore</h2>
<p>Each page has a year toggle: all years pooled, or one meeting at a time.</p>
<div class="cards">
  <a class="card" href="phrases.html">
    <img src="img/{{ 'all' if pooled else latest.year }}_headline.png" alt="" loading="lazy">
    <div class="body"><h3>Phrases</h3>
    <p>Phrases that predict a talk, how they trend year to year, a lookup for any phrase, and sample sizes in talks
    versus posters.</p><span class="more">Phrases →</span></div>
  </a>
  <a class="card" href="institutions.html">
    <img src="img/{{ 'all' if pooled else latest.year }}_institutions.png" alt="" loading="lazy">
    <div class="body"><h3>Institutions</h3>
    <p>Which of the largest institutions have the highest talk rate, crediting the first author.</p>
    <span class="more">Institutions →</span></div>
  </a>
  <a class="card" href="geography.html">
    <img src="img/{{ 'all' if pooled else latest.year }}_regions.png" alt="" loading="lazy">
    <div class="body"><h3>Geography</h3>
    <p>Talk rate by world region, country and metro area, the host-city effect, and where the meeting's center of
    mass sits each year.</p>
    <span class="more">Regions, countries and metros →</span></div>
  </a>
  <a class="card" href="authors.html">
    <img src="img/{{ 'all' if pooled else latest.year }}_senior_authors.png" alt="" loading="lazy">
    <div class="body"><h3>Senior authors</h3>
    <p>Senior authors with the most consistent record of talks, ranked by the lower end of a 95% interval.</p>
    <span class="more">Senior authors →</span></div>
  </a>
  <a class="card text-only" href="methods.html">
    <div class="body"><h3>Methods and caveats</h3>
    <p>How the abstracts are parsed, how institutions and places are matched (and how often they can't be), how
    phrases are scored, talk rates by year, and what the numbers can't tell you.</p><span class="more">Methods →</span></div>
  </a>
</div>
{% endblock %}
